Since I like futility, I will spell out the process from the very start and 
would recommend that OP follows them without deviating from the procedure. 
I'm running Win2k with service pack 4 (pretty much the same as winxp with 
less cruft) performed every step as I wrote it out for this post and it 
works!

Download the NetHack sources
Unpack the sources to c:\nethack-3.4.3
Open up the terminal
cd nethack-3.4.3\sys\winnt (OP did eventually say they're using winxp)
type nhsetup.bat and hit enter

If you already have MinGW installed then skip this step
-------------------------------------------------
Download and install MinGW
-------------------------------------------------

create install.bat per the simple instructions at 
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Compiling
type install.bat and hit enter

There's gonna be a shitload of scary text and messages scrolling forever 
upward as NetHack compiles. Perhaps maybe you might want to begin skimming 
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Patching in the meantime?

It's done! Quickly check nethack-3.4.3\binary to see if the binary 
vanished!!!

Now it's time to patch this puppy! For this example I will use the Enhanced 
Artifacts v1.0 patch. You can acquire it from this link 
http://zindorsky.kundor.org/patches/banes.zip

Unpack banes.zip into c:\nethack-3.4.3
Fire up the terminal if you closed it after compiling NetHack
Type cd nethack-3.4.3 and hit enter
Type path=c:\mingw\bin and hit enter
Type patch -p1 < banes.diff and hit enter

You'll get messages about patching .c and .h files.

Now, quickly, run install.bat

You're going to get a passel of scary stuff when you originally compiled 
NetHack. Once it's done go an investigate the c:\nethack-3.4.3\binary 
folder to see if your NetHack binary has mysteriously disappeared!!! Mine 
didn't!!!

Fire up NetHack, ^W for dragonbane and ^W for a wand of magic missile. 
Wield dragonbane, fire the wand of magic missile against an adjacent wall 
and be overjoyed as dragonbane reflects the beam! Make a note! HUGE 
SUCCESS!

If you're feeling ballsy after this then kindly RTFM and tackle the 
menucolors patch (which I feel can be considered by the average Windows 
user to be a bit daunting for inclusion in a tutorial)

Your hand has been held. Doesn't get any simpler than this.


